  "answer": "n = 40",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Small values of n all give primes, so testing 0, 1, 2, ... by hand takes a while.",
    "Look for an n that makes every term of n² + n + 41 share a common factor."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Take $n = 40$: $40^2 + 40 + 41 = 1681 = 41^2$, which is not prime.",
    "(Also $n = 41$: $41^2 + 41 + 41 = 41 \\cdot 43$.) So the statement is false."
  ],
